  "id": "COMPOUND:21451 - PROTEIN:5866",
  "verbalization": "Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside is implicated in the biological activity of NCI-H446 through a series of target interactions, primarily involving the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit serves as a common intermediary in multiple pathways, with Methyl valerate, Spirostan-3,27-diol, and Robinetinidol all acting as targets that ultimately engage NCI-H446. The evidence suggests a hierarchical relationship where Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside directly targets the 26S proteasome subunit, which in turn is targeted by various compounds, leading to a cascade of effects on NCI-H446. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside may influence NCI-H446 through the modulation of proteasome activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and their shared involvement in NCI-H446 suggests a complex regulatory network that warrants further investigation.",
